<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christian VIII of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1786–1848</span> · Also known as Christian Frederik, Christian Frederick</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christian VIII was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> from 1839 to 1848. As Prince Christian Frederik, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, he led Norwegian resistance to the transfer of Norway to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kiel">Treaty of Kiel</a> in 1814, convened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eidsvoll">Eidsvoll</a> assembly that adopted the Norwegian constitution and was elected King of Norway on 17 May 1814. After a short war with Sweden he abdicated in October 1814.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christian-viii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="Christian VIII of Denmark" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johan Vilhelm Gertner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kong_Christian_d._8..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
